AMIX libc has no mkstemp, so configure builds lib/mkstemp.c, which defines
rpl_mkstemp -- but 2.8.1 uses AC_REPLACE_FUNCS without the gnulib define
that maps mkstemp to rpl_mkstemp, and no header declares it.  sdiff.c calls
it: GCC 14 rejects the implicit declaration, and the link would miss it.
Map and declare it where system.h pulls in <stdlib.h>, only when the
replacement is in use.

--- a/src/system.h	2026-10-29 21:27:38.352545755 +0200
+++ b/src/system.h	2026-10-29 21:28:55.916459119 +0200
@@ -191,6 +191,10 @@
    char *getenv ();
 # endif
 #endif
+#if !HAVE_MKSTEMP
+# define mkstemp rpl_mkstemp
+int mkstemp (char *);
+#endif
 #ifndef EXIT_SUCCESS
 # define EXIT_SUCCESS 0
 #endif
